{
 "id":"03-yawn",
 "events":[
  ["N","What if every yawn sucked in three times more air than the last?",{"title":1}],
  ["N","Math class. Dale is not okay."],
  ["I","And that is how you factor a quadratic."],
  ["A",1,{"dur":0.9,"off":0.35}],
  ["N","Half a liter. A normal yawn.",{"rung":0}],
  ["A",3,{"dur":0.9,"off":0.35}],
  ["N","Four and a half liters. His homework is gone.",{"rung":1}],
  ["A",5,{"dur":0.9,"off":0.35}],
  ["N","Forty liters. Pencils. Erasers. The teacher's coffee.",{"rung":2}],
  ["A",9,{"dur":0.9,"off":0.35}],
  ["N","Three thousand liters. Every desk slides toward him.",{"rung":3}],
  ["A",13,{"dur":0.9,"off":0.35}],
  ["N","Two hundred sixty five thousand liters. The classroom has no air left. The teacher keeps teaching.",{"rung":4}],
  ["A",16,{"dur":0.9,"off":0.35}],
  ["N","Seven million liters. Almost three Olympic pools of air. The roof caves in.",{"rung":5}],
  ["N","Then it got worse.",{"worse":1}],
  ["A",20,{"dur":1.0,"off":0.4}],
  ["N","Five hundred eighty million liters. A tornado forms. Pointing straight at his mouth.",{"rung":6}],
  ["N","The teacher finally turns around."],
  ["I","Am I boring you, Dale?"],
  ["N","The real part: a normal breath moves about half a liter of air. And scientists still aren't sure why we yawn.",{"fact":1}]
 ],
